      "problem": "Plot the curve of $y=\\log_7 (x+4).$",
      "worked_solution": "To plot $y=\\log_7 {(x+4)},$ we apply the following steps:\n\n- Take the curve $y=\\log_7 {x}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14246252/assets/975f58b320e2293dbfaf267a3acfe9187438ae40add3603bac98d142b35c44c1.png)\n\n- Translate it by $4$ units to the left to get the graph of $y=\\log_7 {(x+4)}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14246252/assets/ce5db8eb1adb7e84337427c1c769eabec9cb420b51a7e867f47e8d573c697a79.png)",
